<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia Sept private sector credit rises.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia Sept private sector credit rises.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) said on Friday that private sector credit extended by financial intermediaries rose by 0.5 percent in September, seasonally-adjusted, after a rise of 0.3 percent in August.</p>
<p>For the year to September, credit rose by 11.4 percent, compared to 12.8 percent in August.  </p>
<p>The RBA detailed the change in financial aggregates as follows, seasonally-adjusted in percentage terms -</p>
<p>				    Sept 96   August 96	Yr/yr</p>
<p>    Total credit		 +0.5	  +0.3	  +11.4</p>
<p>    M3			     -0.3	  +0.4	   +7.9</p>
<p>    Broad money		  +0.3	  +0.5	   +9.0</p>
<p>-- Private Sector Credit</p>
<p>    Housing			+0.4	  +0.7	   +9.5</p>
<p>    Business		     +0.5	  -0.2	  +13.2</p>
<p>    Other Personal use	 +0.5	  +1.0	  +10.1</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
